@BillyONeal @ras0219-msft @ValeriaConde @JavierMatosD @vicroms @markle11m @danshaw

The intent is not to change anything about our patch acceptance criteria; merely to document what those criteria are so that different vcpkg maintainers give different results.

- Added eslint-plugin-jest and configured jest/globals as env
- Configured *jest.transformIgnorePatterns* in package.json to fix non-transpiled packages

The code used to test the configuration is working as expected is the following:

```tsx
import { renderHook } from '@testing-library/react';
import { DefaultNetwork } from 'consts';
import { APIProvider, useApi } from '../Api';

describe('APIProvider', () => {
  it('should works', () => {
    localStorage.setItem('network', DefaultNetwork);

    const { result } = renderHook(() => useApi(), { wrapper: APIProvider });

    expect(result).toBeDefined();
  });
});
```

Before configuring jest.transformIgnorePatterns, the error was this one:
![Screenshot from 2022-10-22 11-42-50](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/45130584/197330269-09485ebd-ab06-4a82-abf8-cbc310b41c63.png)

After the introduction of the configuration option, there is no more error, jest is able to run babel on needed node_modules:
![Screenshot from 2022-10-22 11-43-30](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/45130584/197330337-5fa96dd2-7634-4e06-92d4-e7648ca6e7af.png)

Any comment or suggestion is welcome

